tive samples of fourth- and eighth-grade students in the nation, states, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, Department of Defense schools, and <strong>26 participating large urban</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"84b348d98e0a40d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a74c2c5012f00b86\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a74c2c5012f00b86\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"444a4958e4647e98\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, the average fourth-grade mathematics score decreased by 5 points and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2005; the average score was one point higher compared to 2003. The average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"444a4958e4647e98\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4bdb98856f12dee5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4bdb98856f12dee5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6542264db8be8b08\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6542264db8be8b08\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50660552d64311d0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50660552d64311d0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8+target%3D\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ed8f12eb63ac748\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, average mathematics scores for the nation were lower by 5 points at fourth grade and <strong>lower by 8 points at eighth grade</strong> compared to scores in 2019. Average scores at grades 4 and 8 were higher compared to the first assessment in 1990.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ed8f12eb63ac748\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"222369ff687131b1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Achievement-Level Results\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"222369ff687131b1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/achievement/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52fe4b635ba963af\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe chart below lists the percentages of fourth-grade public school students performing at each of the NAEP mathematics achievement levels by states/jurisdictions in 2022.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52fe4b635ba963af\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"11c18ed8e5621262\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"11c18ed8e5621262\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26dc3b3d74251961\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26dc3b3d74251961\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7de5779f9dc56aa3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Data Explorer - ETS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7de5779f9dc56aa3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/profiles/stateprofile?amp=&amp=&amp=&amp=&amp=&chort=2&sfj=NP&sj=&st=MN&sub=MAT&year=2024R3\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88e8069dcd467a29\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFind key data for state/jurisdiction performance on the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) assessments in mathematics, reading, writing, and science at grades 4, 8 and 12 (where applicable). View trends and demographics, download snapshot reports, and compare results for each ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88e8069dcd467a29\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:nationsreportcard.gov 2022 mathematics grade 8 Kansas average score 281 Kentucky 268", "provider": "brave", "count": 8, "tookMs": 14699, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a130cc015b8fe56\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a130cc015b8fe56\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1356ed1060d2e1d8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhen comparing state/jurisdiction average scores in mathematics for fourth-grade public school students in 2022 with those from 2019, the previous assessment year, · Results for states/jurisdictions reflect the performance of students in public schools only and are reported along with the ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1356ed1060d2e1d8\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fd82080a397d05da\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fd82080a397d05da\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84b348d98e0a40d2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2022, the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP) mathematics assessment was administered to representative samples of fourth- and eighth-grade students in the nation, states, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, Department of Defense schools, and <strong>26 participating large urban</strong> ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"84b348d98e0a40d2\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74c2c5012f00b86\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a74c2c5012f00b86\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"444a4958e4647e98\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2022, the average fourth-grade mathematics score decreased by 5 points and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2005; the average score was one point higher compared to 2003. The average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower</strong> ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"444a4958e4647e98\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4bdb98856f12dee5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4bdb98856f12dee5\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6542264db8be8b08\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6542264db8be8b08\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50660552d64311d0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50660552d64311d0\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8+target%3D", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ed8f12eb63ac748\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2022, average mathematics scores for the nation were lower by 5 points at fourth grade and <strong>lower by 8 points at eighth grade</strong> compared to scores in 2019. Average scores at grades 4 and 8 were higher compared to the first assessment in 1990.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ed8f12eb63ac748\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"222369ff687131b1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Achievement-Level Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"222369ff687131b1\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/achievement/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTEN